# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
*.tgz

# Local machine state
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Local config and agent scratch. `.env` is per-developer; `.env.example` is the
# tracked template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md

# Review databases. Diffo's real store is ~/.diffo/diffo.db, but a scratch
# $DIFFO_DB pointed inside the repo must never be committed.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# The clips are NOT ignored. `docs/` embeds the .mp4 files directly, and VitePress
# resolves a raw-HTML src as a real asset import — so an untracked clip is a hard
# `docs:build` failure on a fresh clone, not a broken <video>. They ship with the repo.

# The recording harness. It drives a browser and a pty to film the clips, needs
# Chrome, ffmpeg and a real agent to run, and ships nothing — the clips it produces
# are what the repo carries.
tools/capture/
